---
import Workshop from '../../layouts/Workshop.astro';

const prepare = [
  {
    term: 'Before shift change',
    text: 'An open parts enquiry and the latest reply from the workshop or supplier.',
  },
  {
    term: 'Handover note',
    text: 'A short handover with enough information for someone else to make the next call.',
  },
];
---

<Workshop
  title="Leave a parts job for the next shift | Parts Relay"
  description="Leave the next shift a parts handover that names the open question, the person handling it and the next call."
  heading="Leave a parts job for the next shift"
  audience="For both teams. Self-guided, about 12 minutes."
  poster="/assets/counter.webp"
  posterAlt="Two colleagues examine a broken headlamp mount."
  prepare={prepare}
>
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    An adviser who takes over halfway through a job needs to know where to pick up. Write down the
    last answer, the outstanding question and who agreed to follow it up.
  </Fragment>
  <section class="workshop-materials">
    <h2>Gather the latest reply</h2>
    <p>
      Keep the enquiry and the most recent supplier reply beside the handover sheet. Mark any detail
      that has changed since the job opened.
    </p>
    <div>
      <a
        href="/worksheets/parts-relay-handoff-worksheet.md"
        download="Parts-Relay-handoff-worksheet.md"
      >
        Download worksheet ↓
      </a>
      <a href="/guides/counter/">Read the headlamp guide</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="workshop-agenda">
    <h2>A headlamp job between shifts</h2>
    <p>
      A headlamp can light up even when its mounting tab is broken. If the shop has asked for a
      complete housing and the supplier is waiting on the lamp reference, those are the two details
      the next adviser needs first.
    </p>
    <h2>Build the handover</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <h3>Name the item the shop wants</h3>
        <p>
          Record the job identifier, fitting position and scope. If the technician needs the whole
          left headlamp housing, say so and include the reason the housing has to be replaced.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Separate the answer from the open question</h3>
        <p>
          Record what the technician has confirmed about the damaged mounting tab. Then write what
          the supplier still needs, such as the full reference from the old lamp.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Give the next call an owner</h3>
        <p>
          Write down who will get the missing information and who is waiting for it. Record any
          price or availability already quoted beside the exact reference it covers.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <h2>What the next shift needs to find</h2>
    <dl class="workshop-answer">
      <div>
        <dt>Job and component</dt>
        <dd>
          Include enough information to connect the note to the repair order and the correct side of
          the car.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Latest confirmed detail</dt>
        <dd>Write down the finding the next person can rely on and who confirmed it.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Still to settle</dt>
        <dd>State the question that prevents the shop placing the order.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Person following up</dt>
        <dd>
          Identify the person who will make the next contact and the information they agreed to
          obtain.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
    <h2>Let a colleague take over</h2>
    <p>
      Give your colleague the note on its own. If they have to find you to ask whom to ring or what
      to check, add that answer before the shift ends.
    </p>
    <h2>If the next job is mirror glass</h2>
    <p>
      For heated mirror glass, record whether the backing plate is also required. Leave its
      inclusion open until the supplier confirms what comes with the pane.
    </p>
  </section>
</Workshop>
